### Variables
@baseUrl = http://localhost:5090

### 1. Create room
# @name createRoom
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Study room 1",
  "capacity": 10
}

###
@roomId = {{createRoom.response.body.$.id}}

### 2. Get room
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{roomId}}

### 3. Get a missing room (expected: 404)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001

### 4. Create booking (change the dates to the future!)
# @name createBooking
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{roomId}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookedBy": "ana",
  "startUtc": "2030-01-10T10:00:00Z",
  "endUtc": "2030-01-10T12:00:00Z",
  "attendees": 4
}

###
@bookingId = {{createBooking.response.body.$.id}}

### 5. Get booking
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/bookings/{{bookingId}}

### 6. Overlapping booking (expected: 409)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{roomId}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookedBy": "bogdan",
  "startUtc": "2030-01-10T11:00:00Z",
  "endUtc": "2030-01-10T13:00:00Z",
  "attendees": 4
}

### 7. Cancel booking
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/bookings/{{bookingId}}/cancel

### 8. Add your own requests here for the rules in ASSIGNMENT.md
# Every error below must come back as application/problem+json.
# R9 counts a participant's bookings across all rooms and the database survives restarts,
# so the bookings created below put the room id in bookedBy; that keeps the file re-runnable.

### 8.1 R1: empty room name (expected: 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "",
  "capacity": 10
}

### 8.2 R1: whitespace room name (expected: 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "   ",
  "capacity": 10
}

### 8.3 R1: zero capacity (expected: 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Study room 2",
  "capacity": 0
}

### 8.4 R1: negative capacity (expected: 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Study room 2",
  "capacity": -5
}

### 8.5 R2: missing bookedBy (expected: 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{roomId}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "startUtc": "2030-01-11T10:00:00Z",
  "endUtc": "2030-01-11T11:00:00Z",
  "attendees": 4
}

### 8.6 R2: blank bookedBy (expected: 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{roomId}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookedBy": "   ",
  "startUtc": "2030-01-11T10:00:00Z",
  "endUtc": "2030-01-11T11:00:00Z",
  "attendees": 4
}

### 8.7 R3: end equal to start (expected: 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{roomId}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookedBy": "ana",
  "startUtc": "2030-01-11T10:00:00Z",
  "endUtc": "2030-01-11T10:00:00Z",
  "attendees": 4
}

### 8.8 R3: end before start (expected: 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{roomId}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookedBy": "ana",
  "startUtc": "2030-01-11T11:00:00Z",
  "endUtc": "2030-01-11T10:00:00Z",
  "attendees": 4
}

### 8.9 R4: zero attendees (expected: 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{roomId}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookedBy": "ana",
  "startUtc": "2030-01-11T10:00:00Z",
  "endUtc": "2030-01-11T11:00:00Z",
  "attendees": 0
}

### 8.10 R4: attendees over the room capacity of 10 (expected: 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{roomId}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookedBy": "ana",
  "startUtc": "2030-01-11T10:00:00Z",
  "endUtc": "2030-01-11T11:00:00Z",
  "attendees": 11
}

### 8.11 Missing room with an invalid body (expected: 404, before any validation)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookedBy": "",
  "startUtc": "2030-01-11T11:00:00Z",
  "endUtc": "2030-01-11T10:00:00Z",
  "attendees": 0
}

### 8.12 R5: start in the past (expected: 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{roomId}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookedBy": "ana",
  "startUtc": "2020-01-11T10:00:00Z",
  "endUtc": "2020-01-11T11:00:00Z",
  "attendees": 4
}

### 8.13 R6: exactly 4 hours is allowed (expected: 201)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{roomId}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookedBy": "ana-{{roomId}}",
  "startUtc": "2030-01-12T08:00:00Z",
  "endUtc": "2030-01-12T12:00:00Z",
  "attendees": 4
}

### 8.14 R6: 4 hours and 1 minute (expected: 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{roomId}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookedBy": "ana",
  "startUtc": "2030-01-13T08:00:00Z",
  "endUtc": "2030-01-13T12:01:00Z",
  "attendees": 4
}

### 8.15 R7: starts exactly when 8.13 ends, touching is not overlapping (expected: 201)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{roomId}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookedBy": "bogdan-{{roomId}}",
  "startUtc": "2030-01-12T12:00:00Z",
  "endUtc": "2030-01-12T13:00:00Z",
  "attendees": 4
}

### 8.16 R7: ends exactly when 8.13 starts, touching is not overlapping (expected: 201)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{roomId}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookedBy": "bogdan-{{roomId}}",
  "startUtc": "2030-01-12T07:00:00Z",
  "endUtc": "2030-01-12T08:00:00Z",
  "attendees": 4
}

### 8.17 R8: cancel the booking from 7. again (expected: 409)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/bookings/{{bookingId}}/cancel

### 8.18 R8: cancel a missing booking (expected: 404)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/bookings/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002/cancel

### 8.19 R8: rebook the slot freed by the cancel in 7. (expected: 201)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{roomId}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookedBy": "bogdan-{{roomId}}",
  "startUtc": "2030-01-10T10:00:00Z",
  "endUtc": "2030-01-10T12:00:00Z",
  "attendees": 4
}

### 8.20 R9 setup: a second room (expected: 201)
# @name createRoom2
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Study room 2",
  "capacity": 10
}

###
@roomId2 = {{createRoom2.response.body.$.id}}

### 8.21 R9: carmen's 1st booking on 2030-02-01, room 1 (expected: 201)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{roomId}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookedBy": "carmen-{{roomId}}",
  "startUtc": "2030-02-01T09:00:00Z",
  "endUtc": "2030-02-01T10:00:00Z",
  "attendees": 2
}

### 8.22 R9: carmen's 2nd booking on 2030-02-01, room 2 (expected: 201)
# @name carmenSecond
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{roomId2}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookedBy": "carmen-{{roomId}}",
  "startUtc": "2030-02-01T11:00:00Z",
  "endUtc": "2030-02-01T12:00:00Z",
  "attendees": 2
}

### 8.23 R9: carmen's 3rd active booking on 2030-02-01, counted across rooms (expected: 409)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{roomId2}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookedBy": "carmen-{{roomId}}",
  "startUtc": "2030-02-01T14:00:00Z",
  "endUtc": "2030-02-01T15:00:00Z",
  "attendees": 2
}

### 8.24 R9: another participant on the same day is not affected (expected: 201)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{roomId}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookedBy": "dan-{{roomId}}",
  "startUtc": "2030-02-01T14:00:00Z",
  "endUtc": "2030-02-01T15:00:00Z",
  "attendees": 2
}

### 8.25 R9: carmen on the next day is not affected (expected: 201)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{roomId}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookedBy": "carmen-{{roomId}}",
  "startUtc": "2030-02-02T09:00:00Z",
  "endUtc": "2030-02-02T10:00:00Z",
  "attendees": 2
}

### 8.26 R9: cancel carmen's 2nd booking on 2030-02-01 (expected: 204)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/bookings/{{carmenSecond.response.body.$.id}}/cancel

### 8.27 R9: cancelled bookings do not count, so the booking from 8.23 now fits (expected: 201)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{roomId2}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookedBy": "carmen-{{roomId}}",
  "startUtc": "2030-02-01T14:00:00Z",
  "endUtc": "2030-02-01T15:00:00Z",
  "attendees": 2
}

### 8.28 R9: the day is the UTC date; 02-02 01:00+02:00 is 02-01 23:00Z, carmen's 3rd there (expected: 409)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{roomId2}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookedBy": "carmen-{{roomId}}",
  "startUtc": "2030-02-02T01:00:00+02:00",
  "endUtc": "2030-02-02T02:00:00+02:00",
  "attendees": 2
}

### 8.29 R9: the day is the UTC date; 02-01 23:30 at offset -01:00 is 02-02 00:30Z, carmen's 2nd there (expected: 201)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{roomId2}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookedBy": "carmen-{{roomId}}",
  "startUtc": "2030-02-01T23:30:00-01:00",
  "endUtc": "2030-02-02T00:30:00-01:00",
  "attendees": 2
}

### 8.30 R10 setup: a large room, capacity 11 (expected: 201)
# @name createLargeRoom
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Large room",
  "capacity": 11
}

###
@largeRoomId = {{createLargeRoom.response.body.$.id}}

