POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{roomId}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookedBy": "eva-{{roomId}}",
  "startUtc": "2030-03-11T08:00:00Z",
  "endUtc": "2030-03-11T11:00:00Z",
  "attendees": 4
}

### 8.35 R11 setup: a booking that starts in 30 minutes (expected: 201)
# R11 depends on "now", so these use REST Client's $datetime with an offset from the current time.
# @name soonBooking
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{roomId}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookedBy": "fane-{{roomId}}",
  "startUtc": "{{$datetime iso8601 30 m}}",
  "endUtc": "{{$datetime iso8601 60 m}}",
  "attendees": 2
}

### 8.36 R11: cancel it, less than 60 minutes before the start (expected: 409)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/bookings/{{soonBooking.response.body.$.id}}/cancel

### 8.37 R11 setup: a booking that starts in 2 hours (expected: 201)
# @name laterBooking
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rooms/{{roomId}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookedBy": "fane-{{roomId}}",
  "startUtc": "{{$datetime iso8601 120 m}}",
  "endUtc": "{{$datetime iso8601 150 m}}",
  "attendees": 2
}

### 8.38 R11: cancel it, 2 hours before the start (expected: 204)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/bookings/{{laterBooking.response.body.$.id}}/cancel
